From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Mar 2026 14:41:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sun4i: mixer: Describe scaler types per channel

A scaler-presence bitmask cannot distinguish the VSU10, edge-detection and
VSU8 implementations found from DE3 onward. Replace it with a per-channel
scaler-type array while retaining an explicit no-scaler value.

Keep VI YUV format exposure tied to the presence of a scaler because
subsampled formats require chroma upsampling.

Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
[aiyengar: LibreELEC 0218, rebased onto the older DE33 format selection
 carried in patches.drm/0034 (no yuv_support variable): the scaler_mask
 test in sun8i_vi_layer_init_one() is converted in place]
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
